; slack_negative_capacity: SLACK with a negative capacity appends nothing
; to either vec.
;
; spec/xqvm/ISA.md's SLACK row: "If capacity <= 0, no elements are
; appended." slack_zero pins capacity 0; this pins the negative half. With
; no entries appended, SLACK charges only BASE_STEPS
; (spec/xqvm/METERING.md: entries * 2 * ELEMENT_COPY_STEPS), so the run is
; eight instructions at one step each.

VECI r0
VECI r1
PUSH 0           ; start_index
PUSH -1          ; capacity
SLACK r0 r1
VECLEN r0
VECLEN r1
HALT
